From c3f96134c7df1619058b558a0e2fa66ee8fc5da7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:46:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Render stored image alt text instead of hardcoding titles

Every <img> in the theme built its alt attribute from a title
(product.title, article.title, collection.title, a section heading),
so the alt text stored on each image in Shopify was never emitted.
Each of these now reads the image's own alt and falls back to the
previous title, so the stored text is used where it exists and
nothing regresses where it doesn't:

- templates/product.liquid, sections/main-product.liquid
- snippets/card-product.liquid, card-collection.liquid, coll-card.liquid
- sections/main-list-collections.liquid
- sections/blog-posts.liquid, main-blog.liquid, main-article.liquid
- sections/hero.liquid, custom-process.liquid, page-portfolio.liquid,
  testimonials.liquid

Also fill in three genuinely empty alt attributes:

- sections/instagram-grid.liquid: each tile is a link wrapping only an
  image, so alt="" left the link with no accessible name.
- sections/page-installation.liquid: the hero and the per-step photos
  are illustrative content, not decoration, so they now carry the
  section heading and the step title respectively.

Empty alt attributes that are correct are left alone: lightbox
placeholders filled in by JS, gallery thumbnail buttons that duplicate
the labelled main image, and the decorative login/register side panels.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
